-- title:
--   The relation U· V=π in the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$. Consider the ring of formal power series in two variables $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$, the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W π` generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, where $X_0, X_1$ are the two coordinate variables and $C$ is the constant-coefficient inclusion of $W$, and the quotient ring `UVCrossingModel W π`, i.e. $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi)$. In this quotient, `U π` and `V π` denote the residue classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$ respectively, and for $w \in W$ the element `const π w` denotes the residue class of the constant series $C(w)$. The theorem asserts the single equation $$U(\pi)\cdot V(\pi) = \mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\pi$$ in `UVCrossingModel W π`: the product of the two branch parameters equals the image of $\pi$ itself. No hypotheses beyond the commutative ring structure on $W$ are imposed; in particular $\pi$ may be a zero divisor, a unit, or zero.
--
--   This records the defining relation of the crossing (ordinary double point) model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$, the shape of the completed local ring of a modular curve with $\Gamma_0(p)$-level structure at a supersingular point of the special fibre, with $\pi$ playing the role of the uniformiser $p$. It is used throughout the local analysis of such crossing presentations, for instance in the identification of completed local rings of blow-up charts and in the derivation of height-one prime and factorisation statements from a crossing presentation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_U_mul_V.lean

